<title>JAPAN: Mitsubishi Oil shares up on PNG oil output report.</title>
<headline>Mitsubishi Oil shares up on PNG oil output report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Mitsubishi Oil Co Ltd were higher on Tuesday morning on a newspaper report that it was planning to start commercial production of crude oil from 1998 in Papua New Guinea, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;While there were not many reasons to buy shares, the issue was bought at the opening due to a newspaper report on Monday,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
<p>But he added that buying momentum had already begun to wane, he said.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Oil was up seven yen at 677 by 0047 GMT.</p>
</text>
